 in the community that gender is merely a social construct, and that gender is not determined by chromosomes or biology;* > *(b) questions how someone can logically, or in good conscience, also support Medicare funding of termination of pregnancy on gender grounds if that is their view;* > *(c) finds termination of pregnancy on gender grounds reprehensible, particularly for the value of girls and boys; and* > *(d) opposes Medicare funding for termination of pregnancy, where it occurs on gender grounds.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4987","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2017-11-16/2"}
